{
 "name": "Tank cross-section: Leopard 2A6 turret cheek",
 "category": "armor",
 "description": "Seen from above: the spaced add-on wedge (two 45 mm high-hardness plates with a rubber interlayer, ~60 deg) then the near-square turret front - 50 mm high-hardness front plate, ~600 mm NERA cavity (20 mm steel + 8 mm rubber packets at 45 deg) and a 60 mm back plate (~860 mm deep, like the measured 2A4). Estimates vs long rods ~800-850 mm. Reconstruction from public sources (Tankograd, Below The Turret Ring, Zaloga/Wikipedia, forum analyses); real tank armour is secret. Armour amount = public protection estimate / mass efficiency (NERA ~1.3-1.5, Soviet arrays ~1.17). The explosive inside ERA is an empty gap until explosives are added, and the model under-represents NERA breaking long rods - so a full simulation is penetrated more easily than the real armour; the Tank check uses the estimates. 2D slice.",
